{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are midpoints of the sides of the larger square. If the larger square has area 60, what is the area of the smaller square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e7899c538a174faf9963a60d09886b7fb12ae942.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(100); draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle,linewidth(1)); draw((0,1)--(1,2)--(2,1)--(1,0)--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (1,2), N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (2,1), E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (1,0), S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (0,1), W);[/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"162\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17916a494132c9d56d7a39c3b1af0ab0e3c3410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ 20 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ 30 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Drawing segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the number of triangles outside square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as the number of triangles inside the square. Thus areas must be equal so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is half the area of the larger square which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f24d7ee7466cd6c3437835583dfa092f48558e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 30 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If the side length of the larger square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the side length of the smaller square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd876d599cd6f7e03cfb5e660c91700674f9ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\cdot x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore the area of the smaller square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8870002f74d967d2a79097db4cc974929017ab19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"39\" />, half of the larger square's area, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, the area of the smaller square in the picture is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f24d7ee7466cd6c3437835583dfa092f48558e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 30 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The smaller square forms four congruent isosceles right triangles whose legs measure half of the larger square's side length. Since the larger square has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, its sides measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b1a32fab18c3a6942ddc0e6a0427bf3b952f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{60}=2\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, the legs of the right triangles measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f6d1e000d3e8c4cb552e4905ed41ad2fa540bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Now we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the length of the hypotenuses, or the smaller square's sides. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00a0c00a3fddc8bbf26eba462d64744c0a5942b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{{\\sqrt{15}}^2+{\\sqrt{15}}^2}=\\sqrt{15+15}=\\sqrt{30}.\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"32\" />\nSquaring this, the area of the smaller square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a019b30007d22707b340c72b8f89ed0358853c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 30 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=822\">https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=822</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pfqtAX6AHNg\">https://youtu.be/pfqtAX6AHNg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 8\">2006 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\